#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0376 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "Columns EXACTLY STUDYID/USUBJID/PARAMCD/AVISIT/AVISITN - AND NOTHING ELSE ENDING IN N OR C. AVISITN is the only *N/*C match and is not in _wildcardExclude, so there is EXACTLY ONE expansion, root AVISIT, with AVISITC synthesised absent (so the *C disjunct is dead). Row 1: primary populated, secondary present-and-blank -> FIRES. Row 2: silent. Record granularity -> 1 violation. AVISITN is blank on the fired row and is NOT pinned."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 AVISIT=WEEK2
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVISIT  type=Char
col AVISITN type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | WEEK2 |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | WEEK4 | 4
